Common issue
ICTV is typically more up to date with viral taxonomy than NCBI. This may result in a taxa not being found due to outdated naming schemes. 
For example NCBI may call an organism Herpesviridae whereas ICTV has already updated the family to Orthoherpesviridae. 
Because of this, we recommend joining newly generated ICTV viral family genome sizes with whatever your current ICTV viral family genome sizes file is.

This can be done with a simple join. We have provided a python script to add any families not found in the newly generated text file from the previous viral families text file.
	`python merge_viralFamily_genomeSizes.py -n new_viral_genome_sizes.txt -o old_viral_genome_sizes.txt`
This will output a file called "viralFamily_genomeSizes.txt" that you can now use with as your final viralFamily_genomeSizes.txt file
